\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces (a) Distributed vertical power delivery: $M{=}49$ regulator cells convert 48\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}V to 1\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}V beneath or behind the compute die, so the high-current rail travels micrometres. (b) The synthesised hybrid regulator, a three-to-one switched-capacitor stage feeding a two-phase buck stage, with the rail carried by each branch annotated. (c) Information flow of the framework: converter synthesis and the component library determine an explicit physical stack, which is shared by the electrical, thermal, mechanical and realizability models. The electrical and thermal models are iterated to a fixed point; the converged field is applied one-way to the mechanical model.}}{3}{figure.1}}
\newlabel{fig:system}{{1}{3}{(a) Distributed vertical power delivery: $M{=}49$ regulator cells convert 48\,V to 1\,V beneath or behind the compute die, so the high-current rail travels micrometres. (b) The synthesised hybrid regulator, a three-to-one switched-capacitor stage feeding a two-phase buck stage, with the rail carried by each branch annotated. (c) Information flow of the framework: converter synthesis and the component library determine an explicit physical stack, which is shared by the electrical, thermal, mechanical and realizability models. The electrical and thermal models are iterated to a fixed point; the converged field is applied one-way to the mechanical model}{figure.1}{}}
