\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces Historical cross-domain comparison on the frozen repartitioned pair, superseded by the physical lineage of Table\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {tab:physical}. The backside architecture dissipates $2.37$\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}W more and runs $8.14$\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}K hotter, yet carries a $16.3$\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}\% lower corner-joint displacement driver $\Delta u_{\mathrm  {c}}$ (d) and an $18.4$\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}\% lower stabilised local inelastic response $\Delta \varepsilon _{\mathrm  {in}}$ (e). The temperature difference and the two magnitudes are conditional on the frozen backside representation (Sec.\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {sec:backside-limit}), and the physical lineage of Sec.\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {sec:physical} reverses the sign of the driver ordering. The two are distinct quantities: (d) is a displacement in micrometres and drives the submodel, (e) is the dimensionless per-cycle response it returns. Warpage is peak-to-valley. Panel (f) reports the measured cost of one complete evaluation on 48 cores; the thermoelastic and local solder solves are entered once each, not once per fixed-point iteration. The ordinates of (a)--(e) are truncated, as the axis break marks.}}{18}{figure.9}}
\newlabel{fig:final}{{9}{18}{Historical cross-domain comparison on the frozen repartitioned pair, superseded by the physical lineage of Table~\ref {tab:physical}. The backside architecture dissipates $2.37$\,W more and runs $8.14$\,K hotter, yet carries a $16.3$\,\% lower corner-joint displacement driver $\du $ (d) and an $18.4$\,\% lower stabilised local inelastic response $\Delta \varepsilon _{\mathrm {in}}$ (e). The temperature difference and the two magnitudes are conditional on the frozen backside representation (Sec.~\ref {sec:backside-limit}), and the physical lineage of Sec.~\ref {sec:physical} reverses the sign of the driver ordering. The two are distinct quantities: (d) is a displacement in micrometres and drives the submodel, (e) is the dimensionless per-cycle response it returns. Warpage is peak-to-valley. Panel (f) reports the measured cost of one complete evaluation on 48 cores; the thermoelastic and local solder solves are entered once each, not once per fixed-point iteration. The ordinates of (a)--(e) are truncated, as the axis break marks}{figure.9}{}}
